    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section reports that a 2 \u00d7 2 ANCOVA found no main effects of appearance or interaction, but trait body anxiety strongly affected post-test state body anxiety. It also reports mediation analyses showing that post-test guilt (but not general negative emotion) mediated the effect of the guilt manipulation on post-test body anxiety, with a significant TNIE only for participants in the guilt condition.",
      "evidence_source": "A 2 \u00d7 2 ANCOVA was conducted to assess whether the guilt manipulation, the appearance vs. health manipulation, or the interaction between the two predicted post-test state body anxiety (PASTAS), using trait body anxiety as a covariate. The results fromthemediation analysis, however show that the TNIE was significant (see Table 3 for direct and indirect effects), indicating that there was a significant indirect effect of experimental condition, via post-test guilt, on post-test body anxiety, but only for those in the guilt condition.",
